Admit at most limit events per window

allow() compared the pre-append queue length with <=, so a limiter
configured for N admitted N+1 events before refusing. The repo's own
test_does_not_exceed_limit already caught this (assert 4 == 3) and was
failing; it passes now.

Also correct the class docstring's justification for the monotonic
clock. DST transitions do not move time.time(), which is UTC epoch
seconds; NTP corrections and manual clock sets do, and those are the
steps the monotonic clock actually protects the window from.
